            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48758",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sigstore-core: @sigstore/core: Signature bypass due to incorrect encoding in preAuthEncoding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "sigstore-js provides JavaScript libraries for interacting with Sigstore services. Prior to 3.2.1, the preAuthEncoding function in @sigstore/core uses Node.js ascii encoding when converting the PAE string to bytes, allowing payloadType to be mutated after signing without invalidating the signature and breaking the type-binding guarantee that DSSE is designed to provide. This issue is fixed in version 3.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48758",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48758\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: @sigstore/core\nFixed Version: 3.2.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-48758](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48758)\nsigstore-js provides JavaScript libraries for interacting with Sigstore services. Prior to 3.2.1, the preAuthEncoding function in @sigstore/core uses Node.js ascii encoding when converting the PAE string to bytes, allowing payloadType to be mutated after signing without invalidating the signature and breaking the type-binding guarantee that DSSE is designed to provide. This issue is fixed in version 3.2.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48758**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|@sigstore/core|3.2.1|[CVE-2026-48758](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48758)|\n\nsigstore-js provides JavaScript libraries for interacting with Sigstore services. Prior to 3.2.1, the preAuthEncoding function in @sigstore/core uses Node.js ascii encoding when converting the PAE string to bytes, allowing payloadType to be mutated after signing without invalidating the signature and breaking the type-binding guarantee that DSSE is designed to provide. This issue is fixed in version 3.2.1."
